cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or data, please cite the article. Until it is published,
  cite this software record.
title: >-
  Code and derived data for "Brokerage without bridging: the middle class does not
  connect rich and poor in Brazilian cities"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-22
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/horaciosamaniego/middle-class-brokerage
url: https://horaciosamaniego.github.io/middle-class-brokerage/
abstract: >-
  Code and city-level derived data testing whether any income stratum brokers
  contact between rich and poor residents in directed mobile-phone contact networks
  built from 3.1 billion calls across nearly 300 Brazilian cities. Tier 1 scripts
  reproduce every figure and table from the derived data; tier 2 scripts build those
  data from confidential per-city contact graphs, which are not included.
keywords:
  - social networks
  - brokerage
  - segregation
  - urban inequality
  - social class
  - mobile phone data
  - call detail records
  - Brazil
